# ============================================================================
# JAVA: PER-USER PATHS
# Both point into the profile of the account that opens the shell, so they are
# User scope: at Machine scope $USERPROFILE would be expanded once, to the
# account that ran --admin-setenv. Scoop's gradle manifest writes its own
# GRADLE_USER_HOME (C:\usr\apps\gradle\current\.gradle, lost on scoop update)
# into the User scope at every install; --clean-user-scope removes that and
# applies these lines, in --admin-setenv, --user-install Step 5 and the scoop
# wrapper alike, so every session, elevated ones included, sees the same value.
# ============================================================================
GRADLE_USER_HOME=$USERPROFILE\.gradle
# Informational only (IDE convention). Maven itself reads <localRepository> in
# settings.xml or -Dmaven.repo.local; see the cache section of the system file.
M2_REPO=$USERPROFILE\.m2\repository
